Red Riding Hood went to the garden.
Fruit trees and bushes were growing on the left side. On the right side there, near the well, there was a small vegetable garden consisting of a few beds, which were close to the wooden shed. The shed has gotten dark with time, unlike the brand new barn. The girl walked between the currant bushes, admired the orange fruits of wild roses, which were growing near, and finally, approached the apple trees. There were only three of them, but the harvest was sufficient not only to eat, but to even sell some at the market.